# Invention No. 15 in B minor, BWV 786 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: earnest and searching, the last of the set. The subject
# (after an eighth rest) is a sixteenth turn around B and a falling
# line of leaping eighths with trills, two bars long; under it the bass
# walks in detached eighths. It moves to F-sharp minor, D and A major,
# climbs to a high point and returns home. It wants a measured,
# thoughtful pace with weight on each eighth.
#
# Time signature: 4/4, 22 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI;
# the bass B is on the downbeat of bar 1 (the top enters after an
# eighth rest).
#
# Tempo: quarter = 66, 88 quarters, about 1:22.
# Track times: Gustav Leonhardt (harpsichord, Apple Music reissue)
# 1:21, about 65; Andras Schiff (ECM, clavichord) 1:10, about 75;
# Angela Hewitt (Hyperion) 1:31, about 58; Glenn Gould (Sony, 1964)
# 0:52, about 102, a quick outlier. 66 is Leonhardt's tempo, between
# Hewitt and Schiff.
#
# Structure (read from the Mutopia score and checked against the MIDI;
# the key plan is my own reading):
#   1-2    Subject, top, B minor, over walking bass eighths.
#   3-4    Subject, bottom, F-sharp minor; the top in counterpoint.
#   5-7    Subject, top, F-sharp minor (from 5.5).
#   8-10   Episode: a sequence of broken sixteenths in the top over
#          falling bass scales in eighths.
#   11     Cadence in D major at bar 12.
#   12-13  Subject, bottom, D major.
#   14-15  Subject, top, A major (from bar 14, beat 2).
#   16-17  Rising sequence of slurred sixteenths in the top: the climb
#          to the high B, the climax.
#   18-19  Subject, bottom, B minor: the return.
#   20-21  Subject, top, B minor (from 19.5).
#   21-22  Final cadence on a bare B (no Picardy third), with a fermata.

tempo 66

voice mid 0          # two voices only: there is no middle voice to set back

dyn 1 mf             # bars 1-11: B minor and F-sharp minor, to D major
lead 3-4 bottom      # subject, bass, F-sharp minor
lead 6-7 top         # subject, top, F-sharp minor
broaden 11 0.94      # bar 11: hold back into the D major cadence

dyn 12 mp            # bars 12-15: the major-key middle, a softer manual
lead 12-13 bottom    # subject, bass, D major
lead 14-15 top       # subject, top, A major

ramp 16-17 f         # bars 16-17: the climb to the high B, the one long
                     # build (bars 18-22 stay at f)
lead 18-19 bottom    # subject, bass, B minor: the return
lead 20-21 top       # subject, top, B minor

rit 2 0.7            # bars 21-22 into the final B
